  "curriculum": "The 2026–2027 catalogue identifies the 180 EC Arabic Language and Culture bachelor. The public curriculum gives a 60 EC first year shared by both majors. Arabic Studies then has five taught units of 6 EC, the required Cairo semester of 30 EC, three advanced 6 EC Arabic-source units, 30 EC free choice, and the 12 EC thesis. Middle Eastern Studies follows a distinct regional route after the shared year. The source link formerly targeted the Middle Eastern Studies path; the corrected link is the official catalogue destination labelled Arabic Studies. Dutch is the principal language; Literary Studies of the Modern Middle East is in English, and advanced language and literature work uses Arabic.",
  "progression": "Arabic 1 and 2 must be passed before Arabic 3 and 4. Complete the full first year before Year 2, satisfying the first-year Arabic requirement for Arabic Communication and Modern Arabic Literary Discourse, the 48 EC threshold for Literatures of the Modern Middle East and the positive study advice for Philosophy of Science. The reading list continues the literary-discourse unit. Cairo develops Egyptian and Modern Standard Arabic and regional knowledge, before Media Arabic builds on work there. The final thesis requires research with Arabic sources and reports in Dutch or English. Keep the zero-credit Dutch writing diagnostic and recurring tutoring outside the 180 EC. The catalogue distinguishes the first-year diagnostic from the Arabic language sequence.",
